{
  // T9 P-6 — Host face of the DSH dual-target convention
  // (`build:lib:host` + `build:lib:client`), adapted to our no-build reality.
  // DSH:  `tsc -b tsconfig.host.json && tsdown --env.DSH_BUILD_FACE host`
  // Ours: `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.host.json`
  //        (Node 24 type-stripping loads src/*.ts as source — T4 P-8.6 — and
  //        this workspace has no bundler, so the emit/tsdown halves are moot;
  //        the typecheck half is the whole guard).
  //
  // The host face is THE gate for a pure-host plugin: `lib` deliberately
  // EXCLUDES DOM, so any browser-only global (window/document/localStorage/…)
  // referenced in src/ fails this build. At the dsh host runtime those
  // globals are undefined, so this face pins the real invariant. The
  // repo-root tsconfig facade keeps TypeScript's default DOM lib on, which
  // is exactly why this face must be stricter than `pnpm typecheck`.
  //
  // Phase 4 (P4-T2): omo-commands is host-only for the same reason as omo-agents
  // and omo-hooks — a slash command is a `ctx.commands.register` handler plus a
  // template render, and a skill is a `ctx.skills.register` payload; both run
  // in the Node process the agent lives in. It has no src/client and no
  // tsconfig.client.json; `typecheck:libs` therefore runs this face only for the
  // commands package (see the root package.json `typecheck:commands` script).
  //
  // This is the THIRD application of the P-6 host-face discipline after
  // omo-agents (Phase 2) and omo-hooks (Phase 3), not a fourth independent
  // decision: the host-only reason is the same one in all three packages, and
  // so are the compilerOptions that express it (`lib: ["ES2022"]` + `types:
  // ["node"]` + `include: ["src"]` over the root tsconfig). Only the paragraph
  // above is package-specific. If this face ever needs to diverge from the
  // hooks face, the divergence must be justified here — not made silently by
  // editing one of the two files.
  "extends": "../../../tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ES2022"],
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["src"]
}
